<title>PORTUGAL: Air Portugal pilot accused of diamond smuggling.</title>
<headline>Air Portugal pilot accused of diamond smuggling.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese state airline TAP-Air Portugal has begun disciplinary proceedings against a pilot accused of smuggling 910 grammes of diamonds into the country on a flight from Angola this month, a spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Yesterday we began disciplinary steps with a view to a possible dismissal after customs told us that Florentino Lino da Silva had been caught carrying the diamonds on a flight he piloted from Luanda last Friday,&quot; Alves Fernandes said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said he did not know when the probe would be concluded.</p>
<p>Newspapers said the diamonds would be worth at least $1.2 million.</p>
</text>
